ਹੁਮ ਤੋ ਮੋਹਬਬਤ ਕਰੇਗਾ ਹੁਮ ਤੋ ਮੋਹਬਬਤ\nਹੁਮ ਤੋ ਮੋਹਬਬਤ ਕਰੇਗਾ ਹੁਮ ਤੋ ਮੋਹਬਬਤ\n\nਜਬਸੇ ਦੇਖਾ ਤੁਮਕੋ ਏ ਜਾਦੂਗਰ ਹਸੀਨ\nਉਸ ਦਿਨ ਸੇ ਤੋ ਯਹ ਦਿਲ ਕਹੀਂ ਲਗਤਾ ਹੀ ਨਹੀਂ\nਤਬਸੇ ਹਾਲ ਕਿਆ ਹੈ ਕਹੁ ਕਿਆ, ਦਿਲ ਹੈ ਦੀਵਾਨਾ ਤੁਮ੍ਹਾਰਾ\nਕਰਤਾ ਭੀ ਕਿਆ ਹਾਏ ਬਿਚਾਰਾ, ਦਿਲ ਹੈ ਦੀਵਾਨਾ ਤੁਮ੍ਹਾਰਾ\nਹੁਮ ਤੋ ਮੋਹਬਬਤ ਕਰੇਗਾ ਹੁਮ ਤੋ ਮੋਹਬਬਤ\nਹੁਮ ਤੋ ਮੋਹਬਬਤ ਕਰੇਗਾ ਹੁਮ ਤੋ ਮੋਹਬਬਤ', '\"Hum To Mohabbat Karega\" translates to \"We Will Love,\" and this repetitive affirming hook reflects the song\'s core theme of unwavering love. As the narrator has found themselves enchanted by a significant other described as a \"jaadugar haseen\" (enchanting magician), their heart has become spellbound. The lyrics, rich with expressions of infatuation, detail the narrator\'s obsession and yearning since laying eyes on the beloved. Each stanza echoes the sentiments of a love-struck heart unable to find peace or distraction because of this deep affection. Throughout the song, a passionate tension is conveyed, as the narrator describes physical manifestations of love, such as a burning chest and breaking into a sweat at the mere presence of the beloved. This imagery underscores the overwhelming intensity of their emotions. The song also captures a sense of vulnerability, as the narrator admits to being helplessly in love, thus highlighting the universal experience of surrendering to emotions that take control over reason. Cultural context elevates this story of love depicted with expressive, almost poetic Hindi language, where supernatural comparisons like \"magician\" accentuate the mystifying power of love. The recurring hook, \"hum to mohabbat karega,\" asserts that despite every challenge or hesitation, the narrator\'s commitment to love remains unfaltering. This love story is a classic portrayal of romance prevalent in Indian music and film, resonating with listeners who understand or have experienced similar intense emotional connections.', NULL, NULL, 2016, 1, 384, 0, 'published', 'Hum To Mohabbat Karega Lyrics - Kishore Kumar [Meaning & Translation] - 