('d624bc0a-9af6-426c-a719-f896ddbce6d3', 'Madho Hum Aise Tu Aisa', 'madho-hum-aise-tu-aisa', 'Hum paapi tum paap khandan\nNeeko Thakur desaa\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nHum aise tu aisa\n\nHum maile tum oojal karte\nHum nirgun tu daata\nHum moorakh tum chatur sayaane\nTum chatur sayaane, tum chatur sayaane\nTu sarab kalaa ka gyaata\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nHum aise tu aisa\nMaadho hum aise tu aisa\n\nHum paapi tum paap khandan\nNeeko Thakur desaa\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nMaadho hum aise tu aisa\n\nTum sabh saaje saaj nivaaje\nJeeo pind de praana\nNirguniaare gun nahin koi\nGun nahin koi… gun nahin koi…\n\nHum avgun bhare, ik gun naahi\nIk gun naahi… ik gun naahi…\nAmrit chhaad bikhe bikha khaai\nMaya moh bharam pai bhoolay\nSut daara sion preet lagaai\n\nIk uttam panth suneyo Gur sangat\nTih milant jam traas mitaai\n\nIk ardaas bhaat Kirt ki\nGur Raamdaas raakhho sarnaai\nGur Raamdaas… Gur Raamdaas…\nGur Raamdaas… Gur Raamdaas…\n\nNirguniaare gun nahin koi\nTum daan deho mehrvaana\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nHum aise tu aisa\nMaadho hum aise tu aisa\n\nTum karho bhala hum bhala na jaanah\nTum sadaa sadaa dayaala\nTum sukhdaai purakh bidhaate\nTum raakho apne baala\n\nRaamaiyaa, haun baarik tera\nRaamaiyaa, haun baarik tera\nWaheguru ji, haun baarik tera\nWaheguru ji, haun baarik tera\nKaahe na khandas avgun mera\nKaahe na khandas avgun mera\n\nSut aparaadh karat hai jete\nJanani cheet na raakhas tete\nRaamaiyaa, haun baarik tera\nRaamaiyaa, haun baarik tera\n\nTum raakho apne baala\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\n\nWaheguru Waheguru Waheguru Waheguru (Simran)\n\nTum nidhaan atal sultaan\nJeea jant sabh jaachai\nDhan Shri Guru Granth Sahib Ji…\n\nTum ho sabh raajan ke raaja\nRaajan ke raaja, mahaaraajan ke mahaaraaja\nRaajan ke raaja, mahaaraajan ke mahaaraaja\nAiso raaj chhod aur dooja kaun dhiaaiye\nAiso raaj chhod aur dooja kaun dhiaaiye\n\nRaajan ke raaja, mahaaraajan ke mahaaraaja\nMahaaraajan ke mahaaraaja\nRaajaan raaj, bhaanaan bhaan\nDevaan dev, upmaa mahaan\nRaajaan raaj, bhaanaan bhaan\nDevaan dev, upmaa mahaan\n\nTere kavan kavan gun kah kah gaavaan\nTu saahib guni nidhaana\nTumri mahimaa baran na saakon\nTu Thakur ooch Bhagvaana\n\nDhan Shri Guru Granth Sahib Ji…\nDhan Shri Guru Granth Sahib Ji…\n\nTum nidhaan atal sultaan\nJeea jant sabh jaachai\nKaho Nanak hum ihai havaala\nKaho Nanak hum ihai havaala\nRaakh santan kai paachhai\n\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nHum aise tu aisa\nMaadho hum aise tu aisa\n\nHum paapi tum paap khandan\nTum paap khandan… tum paap khandan…\n\nDhan Shri Guru Granth Sahib Ji…\nTum paap khandan… tum paap khandan…\nNeeko Thakur desaa\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nMaadho hum aise tu aisa\n\nHum paapi tum paap khandan\nNeeko Thakur desaa\nMaadho Maadho… Maadho Maadho…\nHum aise tu aisa\nWaheguru ji hum aise tu aisa', NULL, 'I am sinful, You are the destroyer of sins;\nBlessed is Your divine realm, O Lord.\nO Madho, O Madho…\nI am like this, and You are like that.\n\nI am impure, You make me pure;\nI am without virtues, You are the Giver.\nI am foolish, You are wise and all-knowing;\nYou know all skills and all wisdom.\n\nI am filled with faults, I have not even one virtue;\nLeaving nectar, I consume poison.\nDeluded by attachment and illusion,\nI cling to children and spouse.\n\nI have heard of the supreme path in the Guru’s congregation;\nMeeting it, the fear of death is removed.\n\nThis is the humble prayer of the minstrel Kirt:\nO Guru Ram Das, keep me in Your sanctuary.\n\nO Lord, I am Your child;\nWhy do You not erase my faults?\nA child may commit countless mistakes,\nYet the mother does not keep them in her heart.\n\nYou are the eternal treasure, the unshakable King;\nAll beings beg from You.\nYou are the King of kings, the Lord of all rulers.\n\nHow many of Your virtues can I sing?\nI cannot describe Your greatness.\nSays Nanak, this alone is my plea—\nKeep me behind the shelter of the Saints.', 'ह